//? Title: Gaussian Mixtures: Responsibilities and Tensor Adam
//? Subtitle: Optimise a marginal likelihood with valid masses and positive variances
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Unlabelled observations may come from overlapping populations with different means and
covariances. We inspect soft membership in a symmetric two-Gaussian model, then track
explicit tensor Adam on a small separated fixture. A softplus variance bound prevents singular
covariances, while likelihood and posterior normalization remain explicit checks.
)
\toc

> The method

A mixture sums weighted Gaussian densities; the negative log of that sum is the observed-data
objective. Here the learned covariance is diagonal (one scalar per component in the 1-D example).
Unconstrained mass logits a and scale logits s define valid probabilities and positive variances:

$$
\pi=\operatorname{softmax}(a),\quad v=0.01+\operatorname{softplus}(s),\quad
J=-\frac1N\sum_i\operatorname{logsumexp}_k\left[
\log\pi_k-\frac12\left(\log(2\pi v_k)+\frac{(x_i-\mu_k)^2}{v_k}\right)\right].
$$
\alttext(Softmax normalises component masses, softplus puts variances above 0.01, and log-sum-exp marginalises the latent component.)

Bayes responsibilities are the softmax of the component log-joints. Differentiating J weights
each component score by these responsibilities, allowing the visible Adam loop to fit means,
variances and masses directly. This is direct likelihood optimisation, with O(NKD) work per step,
not EM. Adam does not guarantee monotonic likelihood. We check finite improvement and valid
probabilities rather than require every step to improve. The variance bound is approached smoothly;
it is not an eigenvalue-clipping update. The objective is nonconvex and labels can permute.

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/gaussian_mixtures_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/gaussian_mixtures_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/gaussian_mixtures_concept.tikz > build/gaussian_mixtures_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/gaussian_mixtures_concept.svg build/gaussian_mixtures_concept.dvi > build/gaussian_mixtures_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/gaussian_mixtures_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
